# L §2.1 (round 12) "A quarter ... is 2026-Q1 to 2026-Q4, SDMX's form of a reporting quarter (calendar quarters,
# from January, §4.1)"; L §3.1 `quarter` "A period value. 2026-Q1"; L §7.1 quarters used as dates or keys are date
# literals (rows, governs, asks; LOAD-LITERAL in a def: lit). `governs 2026-Q1..2026-Q2` is [2026-01-01, 2026-07-01)
# (L §4.1 spans over periods), so law 2026-06-30 reads v and law 2026-07-01 reads v2; start_of(2026-Q3) is its first
# day; a period moves by an int (L §4.2), 2026-Q1 + 1 is 2026-Q2; an input keyed by one period index is read at its
# key (L §4.6 step 1). (Writer 8: the built-in index quarters is gone, L §2.2, §4.1 "A quarter ... is a value, never a
# key"; the reads of an input keyed by it are dropped.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input r: int

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026-Q1..2026-Q2
  known 2026-01-01
  r = 1

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026-Q3..
  known 2026-01-01
  r = 2

ask a2: start_of(2026-Q3)
ask a3: quarter_of(2026-05-17) == 2026-Q2
ask a4: 2026-Q1 + 1
ask b: r law 2026-07-01
ask b2: r law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a2: 2026-07-01
  cut 2026-10-01
a3: true
  cut 2026-10-01
a4: 2026-Q2
  cut 2026-10-01
b: 2
  law date 2026-07-01, cut 2026-10-01
b2: 1
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-01
